{
  "ledger": [
    "table surface | light wood plane, horizontal far edge near top of frame, fills lower ~85% | unchanged | static reference plane; all blocks rest on it, reflections/shadows consistent beneath each block",
    "background strip | dark out-of-focus zone above table edge with partial leg/tripod shapes at frame left and right | same shapes, only slight lateral drift consistent with minor reframing as the row grows | no openings/connectivity role; never occluded incorrectly by foreground",
    "placed block row | 2 blocks at 0:00 (slot1 x~130, slot3 x~380) with empty gap between | 8 blocks at 0:08-0:09 spanning slots 1-8 (x~160-910) in a straight left-to-right line | every previously placed block keeps its x-position, spacing and left-right order across all cuts; new blocks always settle into the next empty slot at the right end; no block ever swaps sides or overlaps another",
    "hand/arm | enters from top of frame gripping block at left | after placing rightmost block, re-enters from top-left to adjust slots 1-2 at 0:09 | always connected to arm entering from frame top; motion between cuts is compatible with off-screen travel; emerges on correct side of row each time",
    "block-in-transit | appears only gripped by fingertips, tilted, bottom edge above table | settles into the next empty slot before the next cut | never intersects or passes through placed blocks; occluded by gripping fingers (near side) and occludes table/background behind it; occlusion edges evolve smoothly within each shot"
  ],
  "findings": []
}
